[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58575,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial CD34-positive fibroblastic tumour is a distinctive low-grade neoplasm of the skin and subcutis, characterized by a fascicular to sheet-like proliferation of spindled cells with abundant, eosinophilic, granular to glassy cytoplasm, marked nuclear pleomorphism, a low mitotic count, diffuse CD34 expression, and frequent aberrant keratin immunoreactivity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58576,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8810/1 Superficial CD34-positive fibroblastic tumour</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T18:53:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58577,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>2B53.Y Other specified fibroblastic or myofibroblastic tumour, primary site</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:23:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58578,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> <em>PRDM10</em>-rearranged soft tissue tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58579,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58580,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour most frequently occurs in the lower extremities, especially thigh, followed by arm, buttock, shoulder, and (rarely) vulva {23887307; 26946226; 27636918; 30004071}. Tumour size varies from 1.5 to 10&nbsp;cm but is usually &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm {23887307; 27636918; 28937375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58581,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour typically presents as a slow-growing, painless mass of the superficial soft tissues. A long pre-biopsy duration (&gt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;years) is often noted {23887307}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58582,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 40&nbsp;cases have been reported. Most have occurred in middle-aged adults (median age: 37&nbsp;years), with a slight male predominance {23887307; 27636918}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58583,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58584,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>PRDM10</em> rearrangements have been reported in 3&nbsp;cases previously classified as superficial CD34-positive fibroblastic tumour {30570551}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58585,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are circumscribed, firm, yellow to tan soft tissue masses with a variably gelatinous appearance {23887307; 27636918; 28937375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58586,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions grow in a relatively circumscribed, but at least partially infiltrative, fashion and are composed of highly cellular fascicles and sheets of spindled to epithelioid cells with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm, often having a granular or glassy appearance. Lipidized tumour cells are commonly present. The neoplastic cells show moderate to marked nuclear pleomorphism, often with bizarre, hyperchromatic nuclei containing prominent nucleoli and intranuclear cytoplasmic pseudoinclusions. Despite these alarming nuclear features, mitotic activity is very low and necrosis is rarely seen {23887307; 27636918; 26946226; 30004071}. A mixed inflammatory cell infiltrate is often present. There is morphological overlap with tumours reported as <em>PRDM10</em>-rearranged soft tissue tumours {30570551; 25516889}. By immunohistochemistry, superficial CD34-positive fibroblastic tumours invariably express CD34 and are focally immunoreactive for keratins in close to 70% of cases (most often with the AE1/AE3 clones).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58587,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytology shows cellular smears composed of large, pleomorphic cells with granular to glassy cytoplasm {27432164}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58588,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58589,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> superficial location; large eosinophilic cells with granular to glassy cytoplasm; marked nuclear pleomorphism but a very low mitotic count; diffuse CD34 expression and frequent keratin immunoreactivity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58590,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58591,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 249,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis for patients with this tumour is excellent, with only a single reported case with lymph node metastasis and no local recurrences in 30&nbsp;cases with follow-up. All patients with this disease have been reported to be alive and disease-free at the time of last follow-up {23887307; 27636918}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:25:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]